   "notes": "Walker et al.'s preferred B2-KCl BE1 fit uses fictive V0=53.53 A^3, K0=23.7 GPa, and K0'=4.4. Equation BE1 adds the directly reported alpha0*K0=0.0275+/-0.0009 kbar/K thermal pressure coefficient relative to the 23 degC isotherm. The paper states that individual V0, K0, K0', and alpha0 errors are not meaningful because of parameter correlation, so only the published error of the identifiable alpha0*K0 product is retained. The represented data span 3.18-8.14 GPa and 23-600 degC.",
