   "notes": "Preferred broadly useful B2-KCl pressure calibration. The reference isotherm is the Rydberg-Vinet fit to helium-medium 298 K measurements; the paper writes it as a 300 K term in Equation (2). V0 is a fictive zero-pressure B2 value fixed from the 2-6 GPa observations. The additive alpha*K_T term comes from ab initio molecular dynamics. The paper tabulates neither individual coefficient errors nor covariance, so they remain unavailable rather than being set to zero.",
